meta {
  name: validate scan batch
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/collection/scan-batches
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "batch_id": "0b6f5f0e-3c6d-4d1a-9a7a-1f4f3c7d2e10",
    "binder_id": null,
    "sealed_product_id": null,
    "lines": [
      {
        "set_code": "ECL",
        "collector_number": "166",
        "language_code": "FR",
        "foil": false,
        "quantity": 2
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  `201` at the first send, `200` when the same `batch_id` was already validated (nothing is written),
  with the number of copies added. All the lines enter the collection, or none: no purchase price,
  merged into the entry of the same card, finish and binder. Set `binder_id` to `{{binderId}}` to
  store them in a binder, `sealed_product_id` to `{{purchaseId}}` to add them to the content of one
  of your sealed products. `invalid_request` (400, empty batch), `invalid_quantity` (400),
  `binder_not_found` (404), `purchase_not_found` (404, also for a single card purchase),
  `card_not_in_catalog` (404, `lines` names the cards concerned).
}
